            <div xml:id="d747">

                <pb facs="1019" n="891" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg891"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">863.51 Relief Credits/61: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Houghton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-13T16:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 13,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 13—12:36
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>49. My 48, March 13, 1 p.m. Am confidentially informed, by reliable authority
                    speaking unofficially, meeting of March 30 will accept general terms of last
                    Austrian offer for settlement of European relief debts.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Houghton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
